//
// Normative rule vsip_vsie_ssi (src/priv/hypervisor.adoc):
//   When bit 2 of hideleg is zero, vsip.SSIP and vsie.SSIE are read-only zeros. Else, vsip.SSIP and
//     vsie.SSIE are aliases of hip.VSSIP and hie.VSSIE.
//
// Context:
//   vsip.SSIP and vsie.SSIE are bit 1; hip.VSSIP and hie.VSSIE are bit 2. hip.VSSIP is writable, so
//     vsip.SSIP is writable when aliased. Accessed as vsip/vsie from HS-mode and as sip/sie from
//     VS-mode.
//
// Test plan:
//   1. hideleg bit 2 = 0: with hvip.VSSIP = 1 and hie.VSSIE = 1, vsip and vsie read 0 in bits 12:0;
//     setting vsie.SSIE (and vsip.SSIP) leaves hie (and hvip) unchanged and the bits still read 0.
//   2. hideleg bit 2 = 1: vsip bits 12:0 read exactly bit 1 when hvip.VSSIP = 1 and 0 when it is 0;
//     vsie follows hie.VSSIE the same way.
//   3. hideleg bit 2 = 1: csrs/csrc of vsie.SSIE set and clear hie.VSSIE; csrs/csrc of vsip.SSIP
//     set and clear hvip.VSSIP.
//   4. hideleg = bit 2 only: csrw vsie = all ones sets exactly hie bit 2, and csrw vsip = all ones
//     sets exactly hvip.VSSIP (writes to vsip/vsie bits 2, 6, 10 must not reach hip/hie:
//     https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu/-/work_items/4590).
//   5. From VS-mode with hideleg bit 2 = 1 and vsstatus.SIE = 0: sip and sie read the aliased bits,
//     and a VS-mode write of sie.SSIE lands in hie.VSSIE.
//
// Approximate dynamic instruction count: 573
//

